  {
   "user": "O_oNevermore",
   "message": "an illustration of how value schemas work\n\nwe probably have networks or axiologies in our minds\n\nand they are contextual\n\nfor most tasks or chains of thought you might default to a particular axiology\n\nand for a particular task you might switch\n\nso whether you believe the average person is +EV or -EV says something about a value schema that you have\n\npeople like me walk around thinking \"people are bad\" on an intuitive level when in the default axiology\n\nand when it's in specific areas the schema becomes \"people are good\" (such as when showing compassion or working with sensitive or dangerous topics for example)\n\nwe might not know or acknowledge that we walk around saying to ourselves \"people are bad\"\n\nbut that's the effect that the axiology has, it creates a landscape for your intuition to walk around in\n\nand future conjectures, for all sorts of problems and challenges you face throughout your day and throughout life, always dips into the the axiological landscape and asks your intuition to bring forward proposals and candidate solutions",
   "timestamp": "2026-08-22T11:02:15.951000+00:00",
